"Shennong appears in visions as a jolly, antlered old man built like a farmer."
"In memory visions, Shennong teaches a class of a thousand legendary disciples."
"Shennong's core teaching: each self has one perfect Dao; there is none perfect for all."
"A mortal beast can petition the Heavens directly and be judged by its deeds and oaths."
"The Heavens can grant a devoted, virtuous beast a full, flawless human form."
"Three god-like figures unmade a demon's fleeing soul with a joint technique, Reap the Harvest."
"In an ancient Demon War, demons poured from northern gates until a cataclysm broke them."
"Something vast and ancient, more beast than person, sleeps far north in eternal winter."
"The northern sleeper senses Qi it calls 'gold' resonating from the south."
"Ancestral memory crystals can reveal a sect's true, sometimes mortal-artisan origins."
"Some memory crystals from the Age of Heroes hold spirits that outlived their masters."
